Model attribution

The Apple Silicon runtime uses mlx-community/Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507-4bit,
a quantized conversion of Qwen/Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507. Both model cards
identify their license as Apache 2.0. Model weights are downloaded separately
and are not included in this repository.

https://huggingface.co/mlx-community/Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507-4bit
https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507

The optional Ollama runtime uses qwen3:4b-instruct-2507-q4_K_M.
It is a separate quantization and its results may differ from the MLX recordings.

https://ollama.com/library/qwen3:4b-instruct-2507-q4_K_M

Football data

The included Premier League 2024-25 snapshot comes from the existing ONTHEDOT
database, originally populated through API-Football. It contains 380 fixtures,
20 clubs and 15,188 player appearance records, with original nulls preserved.

On 2026-10-26 the project owner confirmed that they hold the required rights and
approved public publication of this complete season snapshot, its catalog and
recorded Qwen examples in https://github.com/landfvit/onthedot-qwen-demo.
This supersedes the historical redistribution warning captured at export time.
The dataset and model recordings retain their original bytes and provenance.
No broader data license is granted by this notice.

